## Report Templates (pick by audience)

| Audience | Template | Max length |
|----------|----------|------------|
| **C-suite / VP** | `ai-program-manager/references/c-suite-executive-brief.md` | **1 page** (2 hard cap) |
| Director / steering (weekly) | Status overview below | 1–2 pages |
| Board / full portfolio | `executive-intelligence.md` (8-section) | Multi-page deck |

### C-Suite Executive Brief (default when user asks for "executive report")

**Header (only):** `# [Name] — Executive Brief` · `Date` · `Reporting period`  
**Body (exactly four sections):**

1. **Achievements** — titled items (bold title + 1–2 sentence body each; 3–4 max)
2. **Business Value & Value Realization** — KPI table first; numbers at a glance; no prose wall
3. **Risk & Mitigation Summary** — table with mitigation on every row (max 4 risks)
4. **Decisions Required** — max 3; recommendation, owner, deadline, consequence if delayed

**End of document only:** Audience, sources, method (`## Document metadata`).

**PDF:** use `references/executive-brief-pdf.css` (9pt body, compact tables, 0.55in margins).

Do **not** use Jira issue lists, monthly appendices, or program deep dives in the C-suite brief —
those belong in the PM/operational pack.

### Director weekly status (when not C-suite)

```
[ORGANIZATION_NAME] — Weekly Status | [YYYY-MM-DD] — [ON TRACK / AT RISK / BLOCKED]

HEADLINE — [One sentence]

STATUS OVERVIEW 🟢/🟡/🔴 — On-Track / At-Risk / Blocked / Completed counts + 2–3 sentence narrative
THIS WEEK'S CHANGES
RISKS REQUIRING ATTENTION (mitigation required per item)
DECISIONS NEEDED (VP authority only)
RECOMMENDED ACTIONS — P1 / P2 with owner and deadline
```

For portfolio-level ROI modeling and governance depth, use `executive-intelligence.md`.

## Delivery
Draft on `{{report_cadence_day}}` before `{{report_cadence_time}}`. For **C-suite briefs**, output Markdown per
`c-suite-executive-brief.md`, then PDF via `scripts/render-executive-brief-pdf.ps1` (uses `executive-brief-pdf.css`).
Offer chat-ready Markdown first; generate PDF when the user asks for a shareable file.
